<title>USA: America First Financial Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>America First Financial Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key Financial Statistics    Q(96)    Q(95)    Y(96)    Y(95)</p>
<p> Net Income ($mm)	     $26.1*     $5.1  $31.4**    $17.2</p>
<p> Net Income Per BUC	     3.53	.77     4.48     2.63</p>
<p> Net Interest Margin (%)     2.70%    2.56%    2.62%    2.37%</p>
<p> Return on Average Assets (%) 4.72%    .86%    1.37%     .73%</p>
<p>Return on Average</p>
<p>   Equity (%)		   63.21%   13.32%   19.62%   11.46%</p>
<p> Loss Reserve/Loans	     .50%     .48%     .50%     .48%</p>
<p>Net Non-Performing</p>
<p>   Assets ($mm)		    5.7	8.6	5.7	8.6</p>
<p>Net Non-Performing Assets/</p>
<p>   Total Assets		   .26%     .36%     .26%     .36%</p>
<p>Allowance for Loan Loss/</p>
<p>   Non-Performing Loans    159.05%  107.66%  159.05%  107.66%</p>
<p>* Q4-96 results include a net income tax benefit of $20.8 million.</p>
<p>** Yr-96 includes a net income tax benefit of $20.8 million in the fourth quarter, and a pre-tax charge of $10.9 million for the additional SAIF assessment in the third quarter. SOURCE America First Financial Corp.</p>
